Subject: [PATCH] webgpu: a device measured without an adapter has none

Some measured GPUs returned no WebGPU adapter in their capture: two of
the Linux NVIDIA cards and the Adreno X1-45, where requestAdapter()
resolves to null in Chrome 152. Their profiles carried no WebGPU
section, which left the host's adapter in place: on a Mac, a persona
claiming an Adreno X1-45 served Apple's adapter.

The compositor now writes webgpu.available false for such a member, and
the GPU process answers requestAdapter() with no adapter whenever the
profile says so, on any host. Members that measured an adapter are
unchanged.

diff --git a/base/apostate/compose.cc b/base/apostate/compose.cc
index 8ba4c7f..5725500 100644
--- a/base/apostate/compose.cc
+++ b/base/apostate/compose.cc
@@ -1573,10 +1573,11 @@ std::optional<Composition> Compose(const ComposeRequest& request,
       }
       if (axis.axis == "gpu_identity") {
         // WebGPU belongs to the resolved member, not to the anchor: it is the
-        // one part of a capability cluster that is not anchor-wide. Two of the
-        // Linux/Vulkan anchor's four members measured no adapter at all, and
-        // claiming a sibling's would be an unmeasured assertion, so an empty
-        // fragment leaves WebGPU host-inherited.
+        // one part of a capability cluster that is not anchor-wide. Some
+        // members measured no adapter at all (two of the Linux/Vulkan anchor's
+        // four, the Adreno X1-45), and claiming a sibling's would be an
+        // unmeasured assertion. The host's own would be one too, so such a
+        // member claims that it has none.
         const ClaimedIdentity identity =
             IdentityFromProfile(composition.profile);
         const AnchorMember* member =
@@ -1603,17 +1604,16 @@ std::optional<Composition> Compose(const ComposeRequest& request,
               .limitation = std::string(),
           });
         } else if (member) {
-          const std::string limitation =
-              "the resolved member measured no WebGPU adapter, so WebGPU is "
-              "the host's own rather than a sibling member's";
+          MergeFragment(composition.profile,
+                        ParseFragment("webgpu", R"({"available":false})"),
+                        request.union_array_paths);
           composition.surfaces.push_back({
               .surface = "webgpu",
-              .value = "(inherited)",
-              .layer = std::string(kLayerHostInherited),
-              .evidence = "host-inherited",
-              .limitation = limitation,
+              .value = "(no adapter)",
+              .layer = std::string(kLayerAnchor),
+              .evidence = std::string(anchor->evidence),
+              .limitation = std::string(),
           });
-          composition.limitations.push_back("webgpu: " + limitation);
         }
       }
       continue;
